# Ryanair API

> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.

## Documentation Index
- `SKILL.md` (this file)
- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)
- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)
- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)

## Authentication
Session Token (x-csrf) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (4)
- `GET /apps/ryanair/{ryanairToken}` — Authenticate with Ryanair using a token.
- `GET /i/api/trips/user/v1/currentUser` — Get current user information.
- `POST /{hash}/{hash}/verify` — Verify user credentials.
- `POST /i/api/session/refresh` — Refresh the user session.

### Data Read (28)
- `GET /{id}/sodar` — Get SODAR data by ID.
- `GET /api/booking/resources/v4/de-de/res/giftcardcountries` — Retrieve supported countries for gift cards.
- `GET /api/booking/v4/de-de/res/{reId}` — Retrieve booking details by ID.
- `GET /api/geoloc/v5/{v5Id}` — Retrieve geolocation data.
- `GET /api/views/locate/3/aggregate/all/{allId}` — Retrieve aggregated location data by ID.
- `GET /api/views/locate/3/categories/de` — Retrieve location categories.
- `GET /api/views/locate/5/airports/de/DUB` — Get airport details by IATA code.
- `GET /content/{contentJwt}` — Retrieve content by JWT.
- `GET /content/ryanair/de/{deId}` — Retrieve content for a specific Ryanair page.
- `GET /de/{deId}` — Get data by ID (German)
- `GET /de/de/lp/gift-cards` — Retrieve gift card landing page data.
- `GET /etc/designs/ryanair/frontend/partials/extras/vouchers/directives/gift-card-list-item.html` — Get gift card list item template.
- `GET /etc/designs/ryanair/frontend/partials/layout/header/standalone/container.html` — Get standalone header template.
- `GET /etc/designs/ryanair/frontend/resources/aem/station-config/{station-configId}` — Retrieve station configuration data.
- `GET /flights/site-data/enabled-markets.json` — Get a list of enabled markets.
- `GET /i/api/trips/trip/v1/allUpcomingSimplifiedTrips` — Retrieve all upcoming simplified trips.
- `GET /mvm/p13n/flight/destinations` — Get a list of flight destinations.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/footer/{footerJwt}` — Retrieve footer data.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/global-header/{global-headerJwt}` — Retrieve global header data.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/home-page/{home-pageJwt}` — Retrieve home page data.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/lp/content/desktop.de-de/{desktop.de-deId}` — Get desktop content by ID.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/markets.json` — Retrieve available markets data.
- `GET /ryanair3/data/trip-planner/fare-finder-results/{fare-finder-resultJwt}` — Retrieve fare finder results.
- `GET /s/horizon/common/personalization/Usp` — Get user personalization settings.
- `GET /s/horizon/common/privacy/providers/CookiesDataProvider` — Retrieve cookie data provider information.
- `GET /s/horizon/react/component/{componentId}` — Get a specific React component.
- `GET /s/run/fpc/context` — Retrieve flight context data.
- `GET /shared-scripts/common-header/{common-headerId}` — Retrieve a common header script.

### Data Write (7)
- `GET /i/api/account/dataSharing/v1/optOut` — Opt-out of data sharing.
- `POST /api/basketapi/de-de/graphql` — Update the booking basket using GraphQL.
- `POST /browser/analytics` — Send browser analytics data.
- `POST /i/api/dynamicfrontdoor/v1/{v1Id}` — Send data to a dynamic front door endpoint.
- `POST /i/api/dynamicfrontdoor/v1/trendingDestinations/flights` — Get trending flight destinations.
- `POST /s/horizon/flights/common/GetFlightSearchHistoryAction` — Save flight search history.
- `POST /s/vestigo/measure` — Send measurement data.

### Search (5)
- `GET /api/farfnd/v4/roundTripFares` — Search for round trip fares.
- `GET /api/views/locate/searchWidget/routes/de/airport/DUB` — Find routes from a specific airport.
- `GET /etc/designs/ryanair/frontend/resources/aem/searchconfig/{searchconfigJwt}` — Fetch search configuration.
- `GET /flights/from/frankfurt` — Search for flights departing from Frankfurt.
- `POST /a/api/smarty/nearby` — Find nearby airports.

### Media (1)
- `GET /resources/ui/ryanair3.0/fare-finder/maps/map-filtered.geojson` — Get a map of filtered fares.

### Config (2)
- `GET /etc/designs/ryanair/frontend/resources/aem/feature-keys.json` — Get feature flag configuration.
- `GET /flightselect_dist/desktop/prefetch-config.json` — Get prefetch configuration settings.

### Core API (2)
- `GET /` — Fetch core API information.
- `GET /i/api/{apiId}/v1/{v1Id}` — Access a core Ryanair API endpoint.

## Quick Start

Here are a few examples to get you started with the Ryanair API:

```typescript
// Example 1: Retrieving airport details by IATA code.
// This is a common operation for displaying airport information to the user.
async function getAirportDetails(iataCode: string) {
  try {
    const airportDetails = await client.get_api_views_locate_5_airports_de_DUB({ DUB: iataCode });
    console.log("Airport Details:", airportDetails);
    return airportDetails;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error fetching airport details:", error);
    return null;
  }
}

getAirportDetails("DUB"); // Example: Get details for Dublin Airport
```

```typescript
// Example 2: Searching for round trip fares.
// This allows users to find available flights for their desired route.
async function searchRoundTripFares() {
  try {
    const fares = await client.get_api_farfnd_v4_roundTripFares();
    console.log("Round Trip Fares:", fares);
    return fares;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error fetching round trip fares:", error);
    return null;
  }
}

searchRoundTripFares();
```

```typescript
// Example 3: Opting out of data sharing.
// This allows users to control their privacy settings.
async function optOutOfDataSharing() {
  try {
    const response = await client.get_i_api_account_dataSharing_v1_optOut();
    console.log("Opt-out response:", response);
    return response;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error opting out of data sharing:", error);
    return null;
  }
}

optOutOfDataSharing();
```

